THE OPEN QUESTION (b) IS RESOLVED, NOT CONTRADICTORY. tokens/spacing.css no longer contains --sidebar-w at all:
  /* The rail, not a sidebar. These tokens used to describe a 260px labelled sidebar that this
     system has never shipped — the desktop shell is AppRail, a 72px icon rail, and it is the
     pattern every template and screen actually uses. The tokens were the wrong half of the pair,
     so they now describe what exists. AppHeader implements --header-h and MobileTopBar
     --topbar-h-mobile; before this round nothing implemented either. */
  --rail-w:72px;
  --header-h:64px; --topbar-h-mobile:56px; --bottomnav-h:72px;
and that matches the shipping rail: components/navigation/AppRail.jsx — `export function AppRail({ items = [], value, onChange, footer = [], avatar, width = 72, brand, style = {}, })`. readme.md states the same reconciliation: "The desktop shell is the 72px `AppRail`, so `--sidebar-w` (which described a 260px sidebar this system has never shipped) is now `--rail-w:72px`."

The layout standard consumes it. templates/app-layout/app.jsx (desktop):
